			"to": "mathematics/normal-distribution",
			"why": "Fisher showed in 1918 that many Mendelian genes, each adding a little, give the bell-shaped spread of a trait such as height that Quetelet had measured in people: the sum of many small effects that the central limit theorem makes normal."
		},
		{
			"to": "blood/sickle-cell",
			"why": "Haldane, one of the synthesis's mathematicians, suggested in 1949 that red-cell disorders persist where malaria is endemic because carriers resist the disease; Allison's work on the sickle-cell trait in East Africa confirmed it."
		}
